<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Placeholder, will respond within 48 hours.</span></p>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Press&nbsp;X&nbsp;to&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;whatever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>On the technical side of things, there's a few grammatical errors scattered throughout the tale. I'd recommend running this through the spellchecker a few times.</p>
<p>On the narrative side of things however, the whole situations feels&#8230; somewhat contrived.</p>
<p><strong>The Security incident:</strong> While I realize you're trying to draw parallels to recent police protests, the level of outpour over the officer's actions seem rather overblown. Two private security officers called the police, and detained one intruder with taser while awaiting law enforcement. That's not really the same as say, a publicly employed law enforcement officer actually shooting someone.</p>
<p>And even if some outpour occurred, I have a hard time believing it'd be at a level where the entire country and some international locations would be metaphorically up in arms. It'd be heavily localized, city-wide at best.</p>
<p>But even if that did all occur somehow, all the Foundation would have to do is publicly &quot;fire&quot; the officers, and then move them to different Foundation sites. Their continued position at one particular branch isn't worth exposing the entire Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Surveillance/interrogation of POI-5651:</strong> This kind of makes the Foundation sound incompetent. So they've been monitoring the POI all day, they know where he works, they know his forum account, they even know where he lives, and they decided to grab him in broad daylight in the middle of the street? They easily could've just quietly slipped in while he was sleeping and hurried him into a car waiting out back, no need for two cars, a civilian witness, and first responders.</p>
<p><strong>Interrogation:</strong> I feel like the Foundation would have enough knowledge/experience to know torture doesn't work. All it does is make the person tell you what they think you want to hear, and damage a potentially valuable resource (the subject).</p>
<p><strong>Investigation Committee-9812 Log-10</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Callaghan: PoI-5651 had been posting a list of addresses he believed was anomalous or related to anomalies.</p>
<p>Pittman: Freyberg, can you tell us where Site-681 is?</p>
<p>Freyberg: 2330&#160;9th Street, Springfield, Oregon.</p>
<p>Callaghan: He updates the list with any strange activity spotted near the addresses. He was most focused on a single address.</p>
<p>Callaghan: One of our staffers were tasked with making a chronology of our history with Veritas. That’s when she noticed something. When Eta-19 secured -5670, we asked him if he was investigating 2330&#160;9th Street.</p>
<p>Freyberg: Why?</p>
<p>Callaghan: Because all of his posts before the incident were investigating 2230&#160;9th Street. He wasn’t investigating Site-681.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure what this is supposed to mean. So 5651 was looking at Site-681's address, as was 5670, but he wasn't investigating the site and was just looking at the address? But at the first log, you state that the group is both aware of the Foundation and the veil, so presumably they were there because they knew it was linked to the Foundation, but they weren't for some reason?</p>
<p>Do they know about the Foundation or not?</p>
<hr />
<p>Overall, this tale's narrative feels rather vague and confusing, and some parts feel written for the sake of artificially continuing the story. The new GOI fails to catch my interest, as it pretty much feels like a self-aware (or not? see above addendum) Parawatch, both being internet based forum communities focused around the anomalous and doesn't bring anything new to the table besides a lack of clarity regarding the group's overall motive.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

