			<div class="content" id="post-content-4793259">
									

<p>Thank you again for looking it over. I will rewrite it to clear up some parts of the story and be more straightforward with the facts.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide&nbsp;response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I realize you're trying to draw parallels to recent police protests</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I actually started writing this prior to the recent protests. In fact, I tried to write it in a way that it wouldn’t immediately connected to real life incidents. I intended to have the part where the officer punched the PoI after being arrested to be the vitriolic cause of the protests.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And even if some outpour occurred, I have a hard time believing it'd be at a level where the entire country and some international locations would be metaphorically up in arms</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I understand. I intended the effects to be localized only and strayed away from that to increase the risk in the story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all the Foundation would have to do is publicly &quot;fire&quot; the officers, and then move them to different Foundation sites</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought of adding in a short document where the officers personally resigned, both from the store and the Foundation because of harassment, but I couldn’t really find a place to put them in the POV of the MC.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This kind of makes the Foundation sound incompetent</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I had overestimated the effect of “the MTF has determined a period where the PoI will be most secluded.” line. Will rewrite the whole event.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So 5651 was looking at Site-681's address, as was 5670, but he wasn't investigating the site and was just looking at the address?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As far as the PoIs knew, they were looking into a weird bookstore that <em>might</em> have had something anomalous. Their knowledge is only up to the belief that it exists, and nothing tangible other than claims and rumors. 5651 was getting his information from 5670, who didn’t really want to be associated with the group (which I should’ve mentioned).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Do they know about the Foundation or not?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>They don’t. The line where it claimed the GoI had been investigating the Foundation was supposed to be written like the Foundation was analyzing the incident as a worst-case scenario. Everything before that, the group’s goals and the incident itself, were just a coincidence. I also intended to write a note before that where it stated that some information was outdated.</p>
<p>I didn’t really intend on having the group as a legitimate GoI, since I don’t know much of Parawatch and don’t want to open a can of worms over how I depicted them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>some parts feel written for the sake of artificially continuing the story</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Other than the public reaction to the incident, is there any other events that were contrived? I don’t trust my own analysis to catch them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The new GOI fails to catch my interest</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I’ve thought of adding a document of the reactions of the group after the incident.</p>
</div>
